{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-0729"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Non-Ferrous Metal Ore Mining Operations Coordinator"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0729"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :mining/nonferrous-ore
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:resource-stewardship :mine-safety :supply-resilience]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :nonferrous-ore-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "NonFerrousOps-LLM ⊣ Non-Ferrous Ore Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, nonferrousops.operation/build), append-only audit
 ledger (nonferrousops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore). Fixes
 a prior gap worse than the usual deferred-stub pattern: `deps.edn`
 already correctly declared the real
 `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph` dependency in its top-level `:deps`
 map (no fake-dependency problem here), but NOTHING in `src/` ever
 called `langgraph.graph` -- the file previously named `operation.cljc`
 was not a StateGraph builder at all, just a static ops-metadata table
 (`operations`/`valid-operation?`/`operation-info`, grep-verified
 unused by any other namespace in this repo). `nonferrousops.sim`'s
 `run-proposal` hand-chained `advisor/mock-advisor -> governor/check`
 directly with plain function calls. No audit ledger existed anywhere
 in the repo, and there was no CI workflow. Now: a genuinely compiled
 StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide -+-> :commit /
 :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`) with
 `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for
 real human-in-the-loop resume, and a real
 `nonferrousops.store/ledger` + `append-ledger!` (new in this fix)
 genuinely wired into the `:commit`, `:hold`, and `:request-approval`
 (rejection) graph nodes. `nonferrousops.governor`'s six HARD checks
 (forbidden operation, no spec-basis, site record missing/not
 verified, unknown commodity, safety-concern-escalation, confidence
 floor) and `nonferrousops.nonferrousopsllm`'s advisor dispatch are
 reused UNCHANGED -- this fix only wires the existing domain policy
 into a real compiled graph and a real ledger, it does not redesign
 it. Preserved EXACTLY as the governor code (not just its prose)
 computes it: FIVE of the six checks -- forbidden-operation,
 no-spec-basis, site-record-missing/not-verified, unknown-commodity,
 AND `:propose/flag-safety-concern`'s own safety-concern-escalation --
 are folded into `check`'s `:hard?` flag and therefore route straight
 to `:hold`, never through `:request-approval`, matching the
 governor's own docstring header (\"ALL HARD violations ... a human
 approver CANNOT override them\"); only low confidence alone reaches
 human sign-off. `nonferrousops.phase`'s workflow-stage tracker
 (intake -> verify -> propose -> resolved/hold, a per-run stage label
 distinct from sibling actors' 0->3 autonomy-rollout phase gates) is
 reused unchanged and now genuinely recorded as `:workflow-phase` on
 every decision audit fact instead of being computed and discarded.
 Proven end-to-end by `test/nonferrousops/operation_test.clj` (ledger
 stays empty until a real commit or across an interrupted/not-yet-
 approved run, hold-until-approved for a low-confidence proposal via
 the `:advisor-fn` injection seam, governor rejection blocks commit
 for five independent HARD violations including the safety-concern
 flag) through the REAL compiled graph, plus a `clojure -M:dev:run`
 demo runner producing real ledger entries for every scenario. 31
 tests / 127 assertions green (`clojure -M:dev:test`), clj-kondo 0
 errors/0 warnings. CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, sibling-checkout
 pattern for `:local/root` deps) was missing and is added in this
 fix."}
